Committee","date":"12/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"Item 10 ALL Revenue and Capital Budgets 26-27","url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk/documents/s23705/item-10-all-revenue-and-capital-budgets-26-27.pdf","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","date":"12/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"07.0 Revenue Budget 26-27","url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk/documents/s23614/07-0-revenue-budget-26-27.pdf","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","date":"02/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"Budget Report 2026-27 Environment Committee 29 January 2025","url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk/documents/s23615/budget-report-2026-27-environment-committee-29-january-2025.pdf","committee":"Environment Committee","date":"29/01/2026","key":false},{"title":"08.0 Budget Report 2026-27 Housing and Wellbeing Committee 20 January 2025","url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk/documents/s23534/08-0-budget-report-2026-27-housing-and-wellbeing-committee-2.pdf","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","date":"20/01/2026","key":false}],"read_documents":[{"title":"Treasury Management - Annual Report 2025/26","url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25187/Final TM Report.pdf","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","date":"2026-07-13","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Special Meeting","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Full Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-30","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-06-04","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-02","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-13","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Full Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.arun.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Arun's housing stock survey is incomplete and flawed, casting doubt on compliance figures","lead":"Arun Council's Housing and Wellbeing Committee heard on 24 September that the council cannot reliably report on whether its homes meet Decent Homes standards because its stock condition survey is incomplete and methodologically flawed. The consultant's review found the survey was designed in-house with no written guidance to surveyors, quality assurance processes, or consistency checks across three different surveying companies. The resulting compliance figure \u2014 41.9 per cent decent homes, 43.4 per cent non-decent \u2014 significantly under-reports the actual position and cannot be relied on for investment planning. Six hundred and eighty-one properties and 103 blocks remain unsurveyed. The survey also excludes communal elements, balconies and other components for which the council is financially responsible, meaning substantial housing revenue account investment needs are not yet assessed. The council has separately reported improvements in complaint handling, with Stage 1 complaints down 37 per cent and response compliance at 91 per cent against a target of 80 per cent.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 3","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25929/25929.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Arun Council's housing survey data rated unfit for planning, auditor finds","lead":"Arun Council cannot reliably plan or fund its housing investment because its stock condition survey lacks quality assurance, consistent methodology, or complete coverage, according to papers reviewed by the Housing and Wellbeing Committee this week. The consultant's assessment rates the data RED. Of 3,430 council homes, 681 properties and 103 blocks remain unsurveyed. The survey was designed in-house using non-standard scoring with no written guidance to surveyors, and three different companies produced inconsistent results. The council reports 41.9 per cent of homes as meeting Decent Homes standards, but the consultant warns this figure is likely an overestimate because key criteria lack sufficient data. The flawed baseline cascades through the housing revenue account (the separate account for council housing), preventing accurate costing of mandatory upgrades to meet energy performance rules by 2030 and leaving leaseholder service charges uncalculated. A separate Warm Homes retrofit programme is already running at \u00a316,463 per property against a \u00a37,500 budget assumption.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 3","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25929/25929.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Arun's housing stock survey data too flawed to guide investment planning, council hears","lead":"Arun council cannot reliably calculate what its 3,430 homes need or what repairs will cost because its housing survey is incomplete and methodologically unsound, the Housing and Wellbeing Committee heard today. Of 3,430 units, 681 properties and 103 blocks remain unsurveyed. The survey uses non-standard scoring with no written guidance to surveyors, different versions with undocumented changes, and no quality assurance \u2014 three different contractors produced inconsistent results. A consultant's report rates the data red. The council cannot calculate service charge liabilities for 473 leaseholder properties in blocks. It is also missing costs for communal elements, balconies and garages for which it is financially responsible. Decent Homes compliance is reported at 41.90%, but this figure rests on flawed data and will likely overstate the actual position. The council's Business Intelligence reporting of compliance \"cannot be relied upon\" for investment planning, the consultant concludes. Rental arrears meanwhile stand at \u00a31,500,545, with collection at 93.05% against a 97% target.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 3","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25929/25929.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25928/25928.pdf","headline":"Emergency repairs completion rate falls 18 percentage points below target in single quarter","detail":"Emergency repair completion within timescale fell to 80.12% this quarter from 98.83% previous quarter, well below 95% target. Manager notes remaining overdue repairs are increasingly complex. Daily monitoring and contractor KPIs are in place to manage.","category":"overspend","matters":"Sharp performance deterioration may indicate contractor issues or resource constraints; complexity of outstanding repairs suggests potential cost pressures.","figures":"80.12% of 387 emergency repairs completed within timescale (target 95%), down from 98.83% previous quarter","quote":"Emergency repairs completed within timescales 95% 80.12% 98.83% 387","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25928/25928.pdf","headline":"Damp and mould response capability collapses: reports issued within timescale fall from 100% to 20%","detail":"Reports issued within 3-day target dropped from 100% last quarter to 20.34% this quarter. Category 1 hazard cases rose from zero to five; Category 2 cases increased from 86 to 139. Performance data indicates acute operational strain in damp and mould response.","category":"compliance","matters":"Indicates loss of compliance capability in handling damp and mould; risks tenant health impacts and satisfaction; suggests resource or process failure.","figures":"Reports in timescale: 20.34% vs target 100% and previous 100% (6 reports issued); CAT1 cases: 5 open vs 0 previous quarter; CAT2 cases: 139 vs 86","quote":"Reports issued within 3 days of inspection completion 100% 20.34% 100% 6","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25928/25928.pdf","headline":"Outstanding fire remedial actions surge 48% to 2,204; waking watch now in place at three blocks","detail":"Outstanding FRA remedial actions increased from 1,496 last quarter to 2,204 (target: zero). Council has implemented waking watch at Hastings Close blocks after determining existing fire mitigations were insufficient. Procurement of additional fire remedial contractors is ongoing, indicating contractor capacity constraints.","category":"audit","matters":"Signals serious fire safety compliance gap; waking watch is expensive interim measure; contractor capacity issues delay remediation of material fire risk.","figures":"2,204 outstanding remedial actions (target 0), up 48% from 1,496; comprising 35 Very High, 1,643 High, 377 Medium, 149 Low priority items","quote":"we have concluded that the current mitigations that are in place in blocks with fire risk remedial actions were not sufficient at the three Hastings Close blocks and as such have implemented a waking watch.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25928/25928.pdf","headline":"Specialist audit reveals 43% of housing stock fails Decent Homes Standard; investment plans under fundability review","detail":"A specialist consultant identified significant errors in previous assessment methodology. Reanalysed stock data shows 1,234 properties (43.38%) do not meet Decent Homes Standard against a 100% target. Investment plans to address this have been prepared and are now with the HRA business plan consultant for fundability assessment.","category":"capital","matters":"Reveals material capital requirement for housing remediation; HRA's capacity to fund the program is uncertain, affecting future borrowing plans and service delivery.","figures":"1,529 homes (56.62%) meet standard; 1,234 homes (43.38%) do not; target 100%","quote":"The remodel of the stock data using the correct definitions, shows 56.62% of the surveyed stock is decent. This equates to 1,234 surveyed properties not being decent.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Housing and Wellbeing Committee","paper_title":"Performance Measures Report Q1 V2","paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25926/25926.pdf","headline":"Data integrity issues identified as principal risk with further measure revisions expected","detail":"Data integrity listed as principal service risk. Compliance team conducting ongoing data validation and assurance on all compliance areas, with note that this may lead to revised measures in Q2. Mirrors Q1 stock condition reassessment that revealed material differences from previous methodology.","category":"governance","matters":"Ongoing data validation may reveal further reporting gaps affecting financial and operational position reliability.","figures":"Data integrity listed as principal risk; validation work ongoing","quote":"The compliance team are working with business improvement to continue to carry out data validation and assurance on all compliance areas, this may lead to revised measures in Q2.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Arun","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Emergency repairs completion rate falls 18 percentage points below target in single quarter","lead":"Sharp performance deterioration may indicate contractor issues or resource constraints; complexity of outstanding repairs suggests potential cost pressures.","also":["37 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Policy and Resources Committee on 2026-10-01","n_findings":38,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Housing performance Q1 Appendix 2","top_paper_url":"https://arun.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s25928/25928.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":84,"news_drafts_total":3}}